## DESCRIPTION
## Find the solution to a 3 by 3 linear system using the matrix inverse
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Linear algebra)
## DBchapter(Systems of linear equations)
## DBsection(Systems with 3 variables)
## Date(September 5, 2014)
## Institution(Fitchburg State University)
## Author(Peter Staab)
## KEYWORDS('matrix inverse', 'solution')

# update 2022.10.30

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.
loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',   'PGML.pl',
    'MatrixReduce.pl', 'PGmatrixmacros.pl',
    'scaffold.pl',     'PGcourse.pl'
);

Context('Vector');

do {
    $A = Matrix([
        [ random(-3, 3), random(-3, 3), 0 ],
        [ random(-3, 3), 0,             random(-3, 3) ],
        [ 0,             random(-3, 3), random(-3, 3) ]
    ]);
    $det = $A->det;
} until abs($A->det) > 0 && abs($A->det) <= 4;

# pick a random solution

do {
    $x = ColumnVector(random(-3, 3), random(-3, 3), random(-3, 3));
} until Vector($x) != Vector(0, 0, 0);
$b = $A * $x;

$inv = $A->inverse;

BEGIN_PGML
This problem solves the equation [`A \vec{x} = \vec{b} `] using the matrix inverse. Let

[`` A=[$A] \qquad \qquad \vec{b}=[$b]``]

END_PGML

Scaffold::Begin();
Section::Begin('Find the matrix inverse');

BEGIN_PGML

Find the inverse of [`A`]:

[``A^{-1} = ``] [___]*{$inv}

END_PGML

Context('Fraction');
$aug = apply_fraction_to_matrix_entries(Matrix([
    [ $A->element(1, 1), $A->element(1, 2), $A->element(1, 3), 1, 0, 0 ],
    [ $A->element(2, 1), $A->element(2, 2), $A->element(2, 3), 0, 1, 0, ],
    [ $A->element(3, 1), $A->element(3, 2), $A->element(3, 3), 0, 0, 1 ]
]));

$aug_red = rref($aug);

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
To solve this, we write the augmented matrix [` [A \; | \; I] `]: 

[``` [$aug] ```]

and then row reduce it to 

[``` [$aug_red] ```]

and note that since the left half of the matrix is the identity matrix, then the 
right half is the inverse or 

[``` A^{-1} = [$inv] ```]

END_PGML_SOLUTION

Section::End();

Section::Begin('Use the inverse to find the solution');

BEGIN_PGML
Solve [`A \vec{x} = \vec{b} `] by first writing [` \vec{x} = A^{-1} \vec{b}`], then

[` \vec{x} = `] [___]{$x}

Write your answer as a vector, like [| <1,2,3> |].
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Next, use matrix multiply to find [` \vec{x} `] or

[``` \vec{x} = A^{-1} \vec{b} = [$inv] [$b] = [$x] ```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

Section::End();
Scaffold::End();

ENDDOCUMENT();    # This should be the last executable line in the problem.
